1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
The day Uncle Tadesse bought a computer, he acted like the biggest tycoon in the neighborhood.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Rubbing the mouse on the table like soap, he wondered why it wasn't making suds.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,000
When it asked for a password, he commanded it sternly: 'I am Tadesse! Open right now!'

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:33,000
When the screen flipped upside down, instead of checking the keyboard, he tilted his head back to read.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:42,000
His ten-year-old niece walked in and said, 'Uncle, you didn't make the computer angry.'

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
In three seconds she pressed two keys, and the screen snapped right back.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Uncle grinned and said, 'I was about to do that—I only flipped it to test it.'

8
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Technology may change, but Uncle Tadesse's self-confidence never changes.
